{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PPCmJiDCKatn5mwy4kEb6X","type":"tool_result","content":"ls: .claude: No such file or directory\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 victor  staff  96 Nov  1 20:00 .agents\n52: * Loads the specified language and stores it in $g_lang_strings, to be used by lang_get\n107:function lang_get_default() {\n254:function lang_get_current() {\n261:\t\t$t_lang = lang_get_default();\n277:function lang_get( $p_string, $p_lang = null ) {\n * @subpackage UnitTests\n * @copyright Copyright MantisBT Team - mantisbt-dev@lists.sourceforge.net\n * @link http://www.mantisbt.org\n */\n\nnamespace Mantis\\tests\\rest;\n\nuse Mantis\\tests\\core\\MantisTestCase;\nuse Mantis\\tests\\core\\RequestBuilder;\nuse GuzzleHttp\\Exception\\GuzzleException;\n596:$s_add_bugnote_button = 'Add Note';","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc894fb4-ac52-41c2-b5f1-d1f66016e336","uuid":"43c43a6b-629f-4372-b642-0d1f8f541fc4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:00:22.863Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ls: .claude: No such file or directory\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 victor  staff  96 Nov  1 20:00 .agents\n52: * Loads the specified language and stores it in $g_lang_strings, to be used by lang_get\n107:function lang_get_default() {\n254:function lang_get_current() {\n261:\t\t$t_lang = lang_get_default();\n277:function lang_get( $p_string, $p_lang = null ) {\n * @subpackage UnitTests\n * @copyright Copyright MantisBT Team - mantisbt-dev@lists.sourceforge.net\n * @link http://www.mantisbt.org\n */\n\nnamespace Mantis\\tests\\rest;\n\nuse Mantis\\tests\\core\\MantisTestCase;\nuse Mantis\\tests\\core\\RequestBuilder;\nuse GuzzleHttp\\Exception\\GuzzleException;\n596:$s_add_bugnote_button = 'Add Note';","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PPCmJiDCKatn5mwy4kEb6X","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcivGwBRF9z7jsRXyRny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DUgJ4EPPq5TMdDxT6iCEK4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > .agents/skills/implement-change/SKILL.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: implement-change\ndescription: Use when you take a MantisBT task (bug fix or small feature) from description to a verified change, using the fast and full gates.\n---\n\n# Implement a change in MantisBT\n\n1. Find the issue on https://mantisbt.org/bugs. Every pull request must reference one (CONTRIBUTING.md). Note its number for the PR description (`Fixes #NNNN`, see `.github/pull_request_template.md`).\n2. Make sure the tools are ready: `composer run setup`. It installs Composer and npm dependencies and the pre-push hook.\n3. Locate the code. Use [docs/product.md](../../../docs/product.md) to map the use case to its entry points, and [docs/architecture.md](../../../docs/architecture.md) for the layers. Business rules go in `core/commands/` or `core/*_api.php`, not in a root page.\n4. Write or extend a test first:\n   - Pure logic that does not need `core.php`: add a test in `tests/Unit/` and run `vendor/bin/phpunit -c phpunit.unit.xml --filter <TestName>`.\n   - Logic that needs the database: add a test in `tests/Mantis/` (extends `MantisCoreBase`). REST behaviour goes in `tests/rest/`.\n5. Make the change. Follow the conventions in AGENTS.md: tabs, `p_`/`t_`/`c_`/`f_`/`g_` prefixes, `require_api()` for core modules, user-visible text through `lang_get()` (see the `add-language-string` skill).\n6. Run the fast gate: `composer run check-fast`. Fix every failure. Do not skip or delete tests.\n7. If the change touches the database, a command, the REST or SOAP API, or a page flow, run the full gate: `composer run check` (needs Docker, reinstalls the local instance). To run one integration test after an install: `vendor/bin/phpunit --filter <TestName>`.\n8. If the schema changes, add an upgrade step at the end of `admin/schema.php`. Never edit existing steps.\n9. Commit with a short imperative subject, as the history does (`Fix tag cache invalidation`, then `Test tag cache invalidation`).\n10. Add an entry to `docs/harness/log.md` if you learned something that the next person needs. Open a pull request to `master`. Never push to `master` directly.\nEOF\ncat > .agents/skills/debug-local/SKILL.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: debug-local\ndescription: Use when a MantisBT page, API call or test fails locally and you need to reproduce it, read the logs, inspect the data and find the cause.\n---\n\n# Debug MantisBT locally\n\n1. Start a local instance: `composer run dev`. It starts MySQL with Docker, installs MantisBT if `config/config_inc.php` is missing and serves http://127.0.0.1:8989/ (login `root` / `root`). Details in [docs/local-dev.md](../../../docs/local-dev.md).\n2. Reproduce the problem:\n   - Page: open it in the browser and keep the terminal of `composer run dev` visible. PHP errors appear there.\n   - REST: create an API token on `api_tokens_page.php`, then `curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" http://127.0.0.1:8989/api/rest/issues/1`.\n   - Test: `vendor/bin/phpunit --filter <TestName>` (needs the install) or `vendor/bin/phpunit -c phpunit.unit.xml --filter <TestName>`.\n3. Turn on MantisBT logging in `config/config_inc.php`: `$g_log_level = LOG_ALL;` and `$g_log_destination = 'file:/tmp/mantisbt.log';`. Add `$g_show_detailed_errors = ON;` to see stack traces in the page. Then `tail -f /tmp/mantisbt.log`.\n4. Inspect the data: `docker compose exec mysql mysql -uroot -proot bugtracker`. Tables are named `mantis_<name>_table` (see [docs/architecture.md](../../../docs/architecture.md)). Settings changed in the UI are in `mantis_config_table`.\n5. Check emails: the local server writes them to `$TMPDIR/fakemail/` through `tests/fakesendmail.sh`.\n6. Use breakpoints when logs are not enough: run PHP with Xdebug. For REST calls made by tests, set `$GLOBALS['MANTIS_TESTSUITE_XDEBUG_SESSION']` in `tests/bootstrap.php`.\n7. If the instance is in a bad state, start again: `build/local_instance.sh install --reset`.\n8. When you find the cause, write a failing test first, then fix it with the `implement-change` skill.\nEOF\ncat > .agents/skills/rest-api-change/SKILL.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: rest-api-change\ndescription: Use when you add or change a MantisBT REST API endpoint, its request or response, or its OpenAPI description.\n---\n\n# Change the REST API\n\n1. Read how a similar endpoint works. Routes are registered in `api/rest/restcore/<resource>_rest.php` (`issues`, `projects`, `users`, `filters`, `config`, `lang`, `pages`, `internal`). The app and the middlewares are set up in `api/rest/index.php`.\n2. Put the business logic in a command class in `core/commands/` (extend `Command`, implement `validate()` and `process()`), or reuse an existing one. The route handler only builds the `query`/`payload`/`options` array, calls `execute()` and returns JSON. See [docs/decisions/0002-commands-shared-by-ui-and-rest.md](../../../docs/decisions/0002-commands-shared-by-ui-and-rest.md).\n3. Signal errors with exceptions from `core/exceptions/` (`ClientException` for bad input, `StateException` for a wrong state). `api/rest/index.php` turns them into HTTP status codes.\n4. Update the contract in `api/rest/mantisbt_openapi.yaml` in the same change. Then run `npm run api:validate`.\n5. Add or extend a test in `tests/rest/` (extends `RestBase`) and, for the command, in `tests/Mantis/`.\n6. Run `composer run check-fast`, then `composer run check`. The full gate starts the web server the REST tests need, and runs `npm run api:generate` to make sure the Postman, Bruno and Scalar outputs still build.\n7. If the SOAP API exposes the same data (`api/soap/mc_*_api.php`), check that it still works: the `soap` suite runs in the full gate.\nEOF\ncat > .agents/skills/add-language-string/SKILL.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: add-language-string\ndescription: Use when a change adds or edits text that users see in MantisBT (labels, messages, errors), so it goes through the language files.\n---\n\n# Add or change a user-visible string\n\n1. Never write user-visible English text directly in a page or API. Pages call `lang_get( 'name' )` (`core/lang_api.php`).\n2. Add the string to `lang/strings_english.txt` only, as `$s_<name> = '<text>';`, next to related strings. Use single quotes and escape apostrophes (`won\\'t`).\n3. Do not edit the other `lang/strings_*.txt` files. translatewiki.net updates them through automated commits (`Localisation updates from https://translatewiki.net. [skip ci]`), and manual edits are lost.\n4. For an enum label, change both `$g_<name>_enum_string` in `config_defaults_inc.php` and `$s_<name>_enum_string` in `lang/strings_english.txt`. They must define the same values: `tests/Unit/ConfigDefaultsUnitTest.php` checks it.\n5. For a new error code, add the constant in `core/constant_inc.php` and the message in the `$MANTIS_ERROR` array of `lang/strings_english.txt`.\n6. Run `composer run check-fast`. `build/lint_php.sh` checks the syntax of the language file and the unit tests check the enums.\nEOF\ngrep -n \"MANTIS_ERROR\\[\" lang/strings_english.txt | head -2; grep -n \"define( 'ERROR_GENERIC'\" core/constant_inc.php","description":"Write the four skills and verify error string facts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":612,"cache_read_input_tokens":138216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":612},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc894fb4-ac52-41c2-b5f1-d1f66016e336","uuid":"0d8f4cac-8d62-4887-93ec-b65b875e17f2","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:00:49.108Z